WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.200
The weather station, by the brook.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.400
The Sun warms a puddle. Look closer.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.000
Some of the water evaporates into water vapor.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.800
Water vapor is invisible. There is nothing to see.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.300
Air carrying the vapor rises.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.000
Higher up, the air is cooler.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.000
In the cooler air, the vapor condenses into tiny drops.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.600
Lots of tiny drops together are what we see as a cloud.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.000
This cloud is liquid drops, not vapor.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.600
Tiny drops bump together and join into bigger drops.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.000
Big drops fall as rain.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.000
The rain gauge measures the rain as a depth, in millimeters.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.800
It runs into the brook and ground, supplying water to the tree.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.000
Then some evaporates again. No start, no end, and no water used up.
